linux-apps (2.1.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
    - rolling_helper, rolling_config, rolling_flash and rolling_ma
      services, shipped with systemd units and a D-Bus policy.
    - udev rules for WWAN port type detection.
    - FCC unlock helpers for ModemManager.
  * Built with the debhelper sequencer (dh 13); files are staged through
    DESTDIR so the build is reproducible.
  * Packaged as a native source package ("3.0 (native)", version 2.1.9).
    The source tree is self-contained, so no separate orig tarball has to be
    shipped and dpkg-buildpackage succeeds both with and without -b.
  * Restructured the top-level LICENSE file: SECTION A is the LGPL-2.1 text
    covering the published sources; SECTION B is a new Custom Binary
    Redistribution License covering the prebuilt artefacts -- the four .a
    static archives in binary_deb/common_lib/ and the rolling_ma helper in
    application/rolling_ma_service/ -- whose sources are not published in
    this repository.  A self-contained copy of that grant ships next to each
    group of artefacts (binary_deb/common_lib/LICENSE and
    application/rolling_ma_service/LICENSE), with file sizes and SHA-256
    digests included.  debian/copyright declares both locations under the
    matching "Rolling-binary-1.0" license.
  * rolling_ma now lives in application/rolling_ma_service/; the upstream
    "install" helper looks it up there before falling back to the old
    binary_deb/ locations.
  * The per-file license headers were normalised to LGPL-2.1 so that they
    agree with the top-level LICENSE, COPYING and debian/copyright.
    application/include/common/rolling_list.h stays GPL-2 because it is
    derived from the Linux kernel.
  * Dropped the leftover bare permission tokens from the install(DIRECTORY)
    calls in CMakeLists.txt.  install(DIRECTORY) only accepts them after
    FILE_PERMISSIONS/DIRECTORY_PERMISSIONS; written bare they are parsed as
    one more source directory and "cpack" aborted with
    "file INSTALL cannot find .../OWNER_EXECUTE".  Modes now come from the
    staged tree, which the upstream "install" helper normalises to 0755/0644,
    so the CPack and debhelper paths stage identical permissions.
  * The install list is now generated.  debian/linux-apps.install.in holds
    every path any supported (project, OEM) pair can produce, and
    override_dh_auto_install expands it into debian/linux-apps.install,
    dropping entries that matched nothing (dh_install aborts with "missing
    files" on those) and creating the empty directories CPack ships
    (rolling_fw_pkg/, and rolling_helper_service/ when BUILD_DOWN_TOOL is
    off).  The previous static list was truncated by the generator, so
    dh_install installed only the MA helper and dh_missing aborted the build.

 -- Qifeng Liu <qifeng.liu@rollingwireless.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:10:00 +0800
